bin/
obj/
.vs/
.idea/
*.user

# Zips built for upload or hand-off. Windows names a "Send to > Compressed folder"
# zip after the last-selected item, so these turn up under surprising names.
*.zip

# Symbols are never worth carrying.
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# refs\ — NOTHING IN IT IS COMMITTED YET. This is temporary, and S2 removes it.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. The reference model arrived from its own private
# repo carrying REAL framework assemblies, which are the commercial product and
# must not be published. They are still on disk locally, so the project builds
# on this machine, but they are kept out of every commit until S2 replaces them
# with .NET REFERENCE assemblies — same public API, no method bodies, safe to
# publish and enough for IntelliSense and compilation.
#
# Consequence, and it is expected rather than a bug: a fresh clone of this repo
# cannot build the reference model until S2 lands. See reference-model/README.md.
#
# S2: delete this whole block, commit refs/ contents, and narrow the ignore to
# refs/*.pdb.
#
# refs/README.md is documentation, not a framework file, so it is kept.
# refs/FRAMEWORK-VERSION.txt is not: it records the maintainer's local source
# path, which has no business in a public repository. S2 regenerates it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/refs/*
!**/refs/README.md
